  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 1006 PM CST Mon Nov 16 2026\n\nWe'll see a shift in the upper air pattern Wednesday as ridging \nbuilds across the Ohio River Valley. This will result temperatures\nwarming well above seasonal norms as highs reach into the 70s with\novernight lows in the 40s and 50s. Atmospheric moisture will\nincrease beneath this ridge, bringing some clouds back around. By\nthis weekend, troughing will start to build in, finally bringing\nsome rain chances back into the area. The first chance for maybe \nsome showers will be Saturday as a weak shortwave filters through.\nPoP is only around 10-15% right now. A slightly better chance for\nrain will come Sunday with chances between 20-25% as a more \nsubstantial shortwave pushes through. Model disagreement remains \nin how much moisture advection we'll see out ahead of the front, \nwhich will impact how much rain we see. Regardless, any rain is \nbetter than none at this point. A cold front will pass through\nbehind this system, cooling us back into 50s for daytime highs \nand 30s for overnight lows.",
